CAT = "ngpolRights"; SEG = "RTS"
Q = [
("Under the Constitution, an arrested person may refuse to answer questions until they have consulted:",
 "A lawyer or person of their choice", ["The Commissioner of Police", "A traditional ruler", "A magistrate only"],
 "The right to remain silent includes the right not to answer until the person has consulted a legal practitioner or anyone they choose."),
("Under the Constitution, within what time must an arrested person be told in writing the facts and grounds of the arrest?",
 "24 hours", ["48 hours", "7 days", "2 hours"],
 "The person must be informed in writing within twenty-four hours, in a language they understand."),
("If a court is within 40 km of where a suspect is held, the Constitution says the suspect should be brought before it within:",
 "One day", ["Two days", "Seven days", "Two months"],
 "A \"reasonable time\" is one day where a court is within 40 km, and two days or longer as the court allows elsewhere."),
("Torturing a suspect to obtain a confession violates the constitutional right to:",
 "Dignity of the human person", ["Freedom of movement", "Private and family life", "Own immovable property"],
 "The right to dignity forbids torture and inhuman or degrading treatment. The Anti-Torture Act 2017 also makes torture an offence."),
("Under the Constitution, a person charged with a criminal offence is presumed to be:",
 "Innocent until proved guilty", ["Guilty until proved innocent", "Guilty if arrested twice", "Innocent only if they stay silent"],
 "The right to fair hearing includes the presumption of innocence until guilt is proved."),
("A person accused of an offence is given time to prepare a defence and heard by an impartial court. This protects the right to:",
 "Fair hearing", ["Freedom of expression", "Personal liberty", "Freedom from discrimination"],
 "Fair hearing includes a hearing within a reasonable time by an independent and impartial court, with time to prepare a defence."),
("The right to form or join a trade union is part of the right to:",
 "Peaceful assembly and association", ["Freedom of movement", "Thought, conscience and religion", "Private and family life"],
 "Freedom of peaceful assembly and association expressly includes forming or belonging to a political party or trade union."),
("The right to hold opinions and to receive and pass on ideas and information is the right to:",
 "Freedom of expression", ["Fair hearing", "Personal liberty", "Peaceful assembly"],
 "Freedom of expression, including freedom of the press, covers holding opinions and sharing information and ideas."),
("Under section 33 of the Constitution, a death caused by the use of force is not a breach of the right to life if the force was:",
 "Reasonably necessary under the law", ["Ordered by any senior officer", "Used to obtain a confession", "Used to recover stolen goods"],
 "The exceptions cover force reasonably necessary, for example to defend against unlawful violence, make a lawful arrest or suppress a riot."),
("A person whose fundamental right has been breached may apply for redress to:",
 "A High Court", ["The Police Service Commission", "INEC", "A customary court only"],
 "The Constitution allows anyone who alleges a breach of a fundamental right to apply to a High Court in that state for redress."),
("Under the Constitution, a person held in custody who has not been tried within what period must be released, with or without conditions?",
 "Two months", ["Three months", "Six months", "One year"],
 "A person in custody or not entitled to bail must be released if not tried within two months of arrest; it is three months for a person on bail."),
("Arresting a suspect's relative to force the suspect to surrender is:",
 "Unlawful under the ACJA 2015", ["Allowed for serious offences", "Allowed with a CP's approval", "Allowed for up to 24 hours"],
 "The Administration of Criminal Justice Act 2015 forbids arresting any person in place of a suspect."),
("Under the Constitution, every citizen may move freely throughout Nigeria and live in any part of it. This is the right to:",
 "Freedom of movement", ["Personal liberty", "Private and family life", "Peaceful assembly"],
 "Freedom of movement lets a citizen move freely throughout Nigeria and reside anywhere in it, and not be expelled from it."),
("Denying a citizen a public job only because of their ethnic group or sex breaches the right to:",
 "Freedom from discrimination", ["Fair hearing", "Freedom of expression", "Dignity of the human person"],
 "Freedom from discrimination protects citizens from being disadvantaged because of community, ethnic group, place of origin, sex, religion or political opinion."),
("Reading a person's letters or listening to their phone calls without lawful authority breaches the right to:",
 "Private and family life", ["Freedom of movement", "Personal liberty", "Fair hearing"],
 "The right to private and family life protects the privacy of homes, correspondence, telephone conversations and telegraphic communications."),
("The right to change one's religion or belief is protected by the right to:",
 "Thought, conscience and religion", ["Peaceful assembly and association", "Freedom from discrimination", "Private and family life"],
 "Freedom of thought, conscience and religion includes freedom to change one's religion or belief and to practise it."),
]
